        depthWeight derivedBandList) = 74 ≠ 190/3` (`uniform_derived_moves_waypoint`) — the banked
        exclusion, re-read on the band-varying tower;
    (6) ★ THE UPWARD DIRECTION: `bandScreen depth ratio < bandScreen depth ratio/(1−w)`
        (`bandVaryingBandScreen_gt_leading`) — the depth-2 running strictly raises each screened band,
        the ONE-LAW-correct direction from the census-conserving undershoot;
    (7) THE PER-BAND CENSUS-IN-CENSUS SELF-REFERENCE: `bandScreen d r/(1−w) = bandScreen d r +
        w·(bandScreen d r/(1−w))` (`bandVaryingBandScreen_selfref`);
    (8) TEETH: the depth-2 running genuinely raises the confinement band (`depth2_conf_gt_leading`);
        the band-varying-zero-on-high value genuinely differs from the uniform-derived one
        (`varying_vs_uniform_waypoint`); the derived weight is nontrivial (`derived_weight_nontrivial`).

    Statable from no single conjunct alone (non-hollow). ⚠ HONEST GRADE: (1)–(8) THEOREM-EXACT now
    (exact identities / inequalities of `Cut`, no error bar, foundations-only). The FRAMEWORK is banked:
    the depth-2 running is a BAND-VARYING second-depth composition, way-point-preserving, ONE-LAW-upward.
    ROUTE-NOT-YET-FOUND (NAMED, NEVER asserted / NEVER fitted): the individual per-band SECOND-DEPTH
    WEIGHTS of the LOW census-conserving tail (each a closed real, its own band's self-overlap census)
    that would restate the census-conserving endpoint AS `1/α(0)` to ≥15 figures — handed to the ONE
    directed successor. The measured `1/α(0) ≈ 137.036`, the undershoot `≈ 135.06`, the additive
    overshoot `≈ 137.95` / `138.97`, and the residual `≈ 1.94` are REMOVABLE ORIENTATION PROSE ONLY; no
    empirical number in any statement or proof; no weight pinned to any measured value; `s` stays the
    derived `1/8`. -/
theorem depthTwoBandVaryingRunning_landing (w depth ratio : Cut)
    (hw0 : 0 < w) (hw1 : w < 1) (hd : 0 < depth) (hr : 1 < ratio)
    (lowTail : List (Cut × (Cut × Cut))) (bands : List (Cut × Cut)) :
    -- (1) additivity
    (∀ xs ys : List (Cut × (Cut × Cut)),
      bandVaryingScreen (xs ++ ys) = bandVaryingScreen xs + bandVaryingScreen ys)
    -- (2) the framework contains Z5 (uniform)
    ∧ bandVaryingInvAlphaZero (withWeight w bands) = dressedInvAlphaZero w bands
    -- (3) the framework contains Z4/X6 (leading)
    ∧ bandVaryingInvAlphaZero (withWeight 0 bands) = invAlphaZero bands
    -- (4) way-point preserved with zero on the high bands
    ∧ (bandVaryingInvAlphaZero (withWeight 0 derivedBandList ++ lowTail)
        = 190 / 3 + bandVaryingScreen lowTail)
    ∧ bandVaryingInvAlphaZero (withWeight 0 derivedBandList) = 190 / 3
    -- (5) the uniform second-depth dressing moves the way-point
    ∧ (bandVaryingInvAlphaZero (withWeight depthWeight derivedBandList) = 74
        ∧ (74 : Cut) ≠ 190 / 3)
    -- (6) the upward direction
    ∧ bandScreen depth ratio < bandScreen depth ratio / (1 - w)
    -- (7) the per-band census-in-census self-reference
    ∧ (bandScreen depth ratio / (1 - w)
        = bandScreen depth ratio + w * (bandScreen depth ratio / (1 - w)))
    -- (8) teeth
    ∧ (bandVaryingInvAlphaZero (withWeight 0 derivedBandList)
        ≠ bandVaryingInvAlphaZero (withWeight depthWeight derivedBandList))
    ∧ (0 < depthWeight ∧ depthWeight < 1) :=
  ⟨bandVaryingScreen_append,
   bandVaryingInvAlphaZero_uniform w (le_of_lt hw0) hw1 bands,
   bandVaryingInvAlphaZero_zeroWeights bands,
   highBands_preserved lowTail,
   zeroOnHigh_preserves_waypoint,
   uniform_derived_moves_waypoint,
   bandVaryingBandScreen_gt_leading w depth ratio hw0 hw1 hd hr,
   bandVaryingBandScreen_selfref w depth ratio hw1,
   varying_vs_uniform_waypoint,
   derived_weight_nontrivial⟩

end

end Phys.Algebra.DepthTwoBandVaryingRunning
